From 50147fffcb108bb08c3fcd58b2647a36d9961463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:57:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(host-contracts): ACL v0.9.0 with the E1 successor
 extension (lifecycle Level 2)

Extension E1 of the Decryption Authority Lifecycle draft, appended to the
retirement namespace fhevm.storage.ACLRetirement (a two-slot Succession
record and a raise-only per-account delay):

- designateSuccessor / acceptSuccession (mandatory, by the successor) /
  confirmSuccessor (at or after confirmableAt = designation time + D,
  D = 7 days) lock a successor; cancelSuccessorDesignation clears a pending
  one; only the successor can clear a confirmed one (resignSuccession).
- retireAccount voids any pending designation, freezes the record and
  emits AccountRetired(account, confirmedSuccessor).
- After retirement, both delegated views answer for (account, successor)
  as an active, non-expiring wildcard delegation would; every other
  delegate gets false; no use, grant, publication or transitivity.
- ERC-165: E1 0x7dc5e209 and the per-account delay 0xc61ca396.
- Version 0.8.0 -> 0.9.0, reinitializer 9 -> 10, reinitializeV9().

Level 0 upgrade tests now run against an ACL v0.8.0 fixture (generated by
make_fixtures.py from lifecycle/level0, blob a0758fb0); new U8 tests cover
v0.8.0 -> v0.9.0, v0.7.0 -> v0.9.0, reinitializeV9 and a Core-only rollback
(fail-closed, record kept). Version pins follow the bump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
